{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "thought\nI have completed a thorough review of all provided materials, including the inventor's disclosure, conversation, drafting brief, and the complete draft application (title, field, background, summary, drawings, detailed description, claims, abstract, and numeral list), as well as all figure briefs.\n\nMy process was as follows:\n1.  I first read and internalized the inventor's disclosure (`input/disclosure.md` and `input/conversation.md`) as the sole source of truth for the technical invention.\n2.  I then systematically reviewed every piece of the draft application and every figure brief.\n3.  For each technical feature, limitation, numbered part, relationship, and method step in the draft, I traced it back to a specific, affirmative statement in the inventor's disclosure.\n4.  I checked for internal consistency across the claims, description, and figure briefs.\n5.  I specifically checked the figure briefs to ensure that any geometric choices not explicitly detailed by the inventor were correctly identified as \"schematic\" and did not introduce unsupported technical substance, per the review instructions.\n\nDuring this process, I identified one critical disclosure fidelity issue in the figure brief for FIG. 5. The brief incorrectly described the relationship between the follower and the cam ring, stating the follower lies \"on this band\" rather than being \"received in a respective oblique slot\" as specified by the inventor. This misrepresents the fundamental pin-in-slot mechanism.\n\nI have formulated a finding that details this error, provides the evidence from both the draft and the source disclosure, and includes a precise, automated fix to correct the text in `figures/FIG-5.md`.\n\nNo other source fidelity or internal consistency issues were found. The claims, detailed description, numerals, and other figure briefs are all well-supported by the inventor's disclosure. The draft is otherwise internally consistent.\n\nI will now submit the results, including the single finding.\nI have completed a full source-fidelity review of the entire patent application draft, including all claims, the detailed description, the abstract, all figure briefs, and the list of reference numerals. Every technical assertion, numbered part, and claimed limitation was traced back to the affirmative inventor disclosure in `input/disclosure.md` and `input/conversation.md`. The draft was also checked for internal consistency.\n\nOne critical disclosure fidelity error was found in the geometry description for FIG. 5, where the relationship between the follower and the cam ring was misstated, contradicting the inventor's description of a pin-in-slot mechanism. A finding has been prepared with a specific fix to correct this error. Apart from this single issue, the remainder of the application is fully supported by the source material and is internally consistent."}
